# Social clips are never muted
- Every clip posted to TikTok, YouTube, or any video channel (tips, live runs, requested reviews) speaks in one of six languages in turn (en, es, pt, de, fr, it; woman, then man) over `media/url-review-demos/bed.wav`. Card text and captions match the clip's language.
- Voices are the natural, upbeat Microsoft neural voices in `scripts/tips-studio/build.js` (edge-tts). Never Piper or other robotic voices.
- One voice and one language for a clip's whole voice-over (#1691). Use single-language voices only: a `*Multilingual*` voice guesses the language of each scene and switched a French clip to English mid-clip. Spanish speaks in a LATAM voice (es-MX Dalia, Jorge). English terms a voice says wrong (deploy, Lighthouse, staging) go in `SAY_AS`, which changes only what the voice reads, never the card text.
- Each clip is a scene clip (#1619): hook, why, look, a "Did you know?" fact, fix, end, about 30 to 55 s, every scene voiced in the clip's language. A post without a `more:` fact skips that scene. A translated clip never voices an English line; one missing its translated title, body or action goes out in English as a whole.
- Render through `scripts/tips-studio/build.js`; it translates, voices, and fails on a silent clip. Before uploading anything else, check `ffmpeg -af volumedetect` shows a peak above -30 dB.
- If Google's free translator rate-limits, fill `<batch>/i18n.json` by agent in `translate.py`'s format.
- Exception, skits (#1041): Gemini (Veo) actors speak the scene in their own voices, so no edge-tts voice. Each skit is made in all six languages, one Gemini take per language, with captions in the take's language. Render through `scripts/skits-studio/build.js`: it lays the bed under the dialogue and fails on a clip whose peak is not above -30 dB.
- Exception, owner shares (#1420): a video Carlos shares from Jarvis (app or web) posts as-is, in the language he speaks in it, with captions in the language he wrote. No edge-tts voice and no six-language cycle. `scripts/social-inbox.js` (run by `social-inbox.yml`) lays it on a blurred 1080x1920 backdrop and fails on a clip whose peak is not above -30 dB.
